# Embedding and Referencing in a Shared Environment:
 @  why sharding ?

1) data set grows too large.
2) Read and Write operations are too intensive for a  single server.
3) Requires better distribution and performance across multiple servers.
4) 






Sharding : horizontal scaling:
.> It is an process of distributing data across multiple servers, called shards.
here each SHARD contains the different set of data, the amount of data that each shard needs to get will determine by the sharding key.
.> shard key : It is an single index fields {userId:1}  or multiple index filed { userId:1, orderDate:1 } 
.> We will create the shard key's and mongodb  will chooses the chunks.
.> One the chunks are decided then they are evenly distributted across the shards.

we have the two stratege to work on here in this case:
1) Embed : In this the parent Document has itself the child docs 
2) Reference : In this we have the parent Doc, and all the child docs will be referenced to the parent doc.
.> Data is distributed differently across shards if we embed or reference.

when to use the embed:?
------------------------------ >
.> Embed data that is frequently accessed together.
.> Reduce complex joins and improve read performance.


when to use the reference:?
----------------------------- >
.> Reference is related data is accessed independently.
.> It can also help avoid bloated documents and unbounded arrays.




